        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(chat): prevent reasoning races after model changes",
        "body": "Closes #106218\n\nAI-assisted: Codex implementation and review; maintainer-directed scope and landing.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users selecting a new chat model and then one of its supported reasoning levels could see the reasoning change rejected against the previously selected model. A send started immediately afterward could also race model-dependent settings.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nModel, reasoning, and speed changes now share one per-session transaction lane in the Control UI. The shared Apple chat view model and Android controller use the same model/reasoning ordering boundary, and sends wait until both the Gateway patch and client reconciliation finish. Production iOS and macOS transports also expose one atomic session-settings patch contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can switch from Claude Fable to GPT-5.6 Sol, select Ultra, and send immediately without Ultra being validated against Fable. macOS, iOS, Android, and the Control UI now preserve the same per-session settings order.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: observed `thinkingLevel \"ultra\" is not supported for anthropic/claude-fable-5` while GPT-5.6 Sol was visibly selected.\n- Control UI unit tests: 445 passed across `chat-command-executor.test.ts`, `chat-view.test.ts`, and `chat-send.test.ts` on patch-equivalent head `21b541785af`.\n- Chromium Control UI E2E: all 44 chat-flow cases passed, including provider-specific Fable -> Sol -> Ultra selection and send waiting for reasoning/speed reconciliation.\n- Shared Apple: 277 focused tests passed: 205 chat view-model tests, 15 shared request/codec tests, and 57 gateway-session route tests.\n- iOS simulator: 11/11 `IOSGatewayChatTransportTests` passed, including the normalized selected-agent thinking patch path.\n- macOS: `swift build --package-path apps/macos --configuration debug` passed.\n- Signed macOS live smoke: Developer ID bundle for head `80dc9d7ac53` launched successfully, stayed alive, and the managed attach-only job was restored.\n- Android: `ChatControllerModelSelectionTest`, `ChatControllerOutboxTest`, and `GatewaySessionReconnectTest` passed, including model/reasoning/send ordering, reconnect replay, and stale-completion coverage.\n- Native localization inventory, all 21 locale artifacts, and generated Android XML/Kotlin resources validate.\n- Fresh autoreview: no actionable findings; generated Android resources correct with 0.99 confidence.\n- Blacksmith Testbox: `tbx_01kxe4ge4ghpc902fsnm2ykc0e` on exact head `d152d46a85c`.\n- Deadcode export baseline: remote check passed after replacing the retired picker export with the settings-lane export.\n- Final rebase range-diff: all seven commits remained patch-identical at head `31239217cbc`.\n",
        "branch": "codex/session-settings-transactions",
